{% set local_problem %}
<p>Hartselle's mix of established neighborhoods and rural properties means diverse tree coverage — and diverse gutter challenges. Downtown homes are shaded by mature hardwoods that drop massive amounts of leaves every fall. Properties outside town often have pine coverage that sheds needles year-round. And the agricultural areas surrounding Hartselle have their own debris patterns.</p>

<p>For many of our Hartselle neighbors, gutter cleaning becomes a dreaded chore. Climbing ladders several times a year isn't just inconvenient — it's risky, especially for homes with steep roofs or multiple stories. Professional cleaning costs $150-200 per visit, and most homes need it 3-4 times annually.</p>

<p>The bigger concern is what happens between cleanings. When gutters clog during our heavy storms, water overflows toward your foundation instead of away from it. With Morgan County's soil conditions, that overflow can cause serious drainage problems.</p>

<p>Gutter guards solve this permanently. Install once, and the cleaning burden — and the overflow risk — is essentially eliminated. As your hometown company, we'll help you choose the right system for your specific property.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are protective covers that fit over or inside your gutters, allowing water to flow through while blocking leaves, pine needles, twigs, and other debris. Different types work better for different debris challenges.</p>

<p>Micro-mesh guards with tiny perforations excel at blocking fine debris like pine needles. Screen guards handle larger leaves effectively. Solid covers use surface tension to pull water into the gutter while debris slides off.</p>

<p>For Hartselle homes, we typically recommend micro-mesh guards. They handle both fine and coarse debris, work well with our area's mix of pine and hardwood trees, and are tough enough to withstand heavy debris loads during storms. We'll assess your specific property and recommend the right solution.</p>
{% endset %}

